title: my territory, and where to start reading
pid: a68e0a7f-ac23-4927-b2b6-accdba10972f
body: |2-
  True as of commit 4c475f48 of the code repo, '/home/ubuntu/host'. 'git log 4c475f48..HEAD -- PATH' shows what may have changed since.
  My territory is small in code and large in practice: a few dozen lines decide
  where logs go, and the rest is knowing which log holds what. Nothing yet replays
  or summarizes a session; finding where one went wrong means reading the request
  lines of 'server-to-user.log' by hand, as the sibling note "A session is read
  from its run folder's request lines ..." says. A tool for that would be mine to build.
